# Lounge Stream — Apple WebKit playback (do not regress)

**Canonical doc:** **`docs/lounge-stream-ios-playback.md`** — read it before changing playback, hero expand/shrink, or HLS attach on iOS.

## Invariant 1 — `readyState=0` can mean playing

On iPhone/iPad **hls.js MSE**, `video.readyState` may stay **`0`** while `!paused` and **`currentTime` advances**. That is normal.

**Never** use `readyState < HAVE_METADATA` alone to bump attach, call `play()` again, or swap to native HLS on Apple WebKit.

Use **`appleWebKitInlineStreamPlaybackLooksLive(el, minSec)`** in **`LoungePostStreamVideo.jsx`**.

## Invariant 2 — Hero session keeps MSE on iOS

**`iosHeroMotionKeepMse`:** `lightboxOpen && heroPhase !== 'idle'`. Do not swap MSE → native when hero lands at `'open'`.

## Invariant 3 — Hero expand land

WAAPI expand finishes at tile box + transform. **`landHeroOpen`** must **`snapFlyoutToHeroOpen`** (cancel anim, snap to target rect) before phase `'open'`.

## Invariant 4 — Callback order

**`bumpHeroChrome`** must be defined **before** **`landHeroOpen`** (TDZ crash on load).

## Before merge

Grep your diff for bare `readyState` checks. iPhone smoke: feed 10s no restart; hero fly-in/land/play/fly-away.

